---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Pneumatic Actuators for Water Treatment | WTP & Wastewater | PNEUMACTUATOR"
  description="Durable pneumatic valve actuators for water treatment plants and wastewater facilities: weatherproof quarter-turn actuation for filter backwash, chemical dosing and sludge lines, with position feedback options."
>
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">INDUSTRIES · WATER TREATMENT</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Pneumatic Actuators for Water Treatment Plants</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Weatherproof quarter-turn actuation for drinking water and wastewater valves — filter backwash, chemical dosing, aeration and sludge services, sized for outdoor duty.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <!-- 应用背景 -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">APPLICATION BACKGROUND</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Keeping Water Plants Running with Automated Valves</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Drinking water plants (WTP) and wastewater facilities automate valves across the whole process: filter backwash sequencing, chemical dosing, aeration control, sludge handling and raw water isolation. Much of this is PLC-driven on-off duty that runs around the clock, and the valves behind it — butterfly and ball valves in most services — are automated with pneumatic actuators because the plants need dependable, repeatable operation with modest maintenance budgets.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The environment is the defining factor in water treatment actuation. Much of the equipment is installed outdoors, in valve pits, or in damp pump rooms, exposed to rain, humidity, UV and regular washdown splash. Corrosion protection therefore matters as much as torque: epoxy-coated housings, stainless steel fasteners, and sealed switch enclosures are standard choices, and chemical dosing areas add exposure to aggressive agents that the actuator materials must tolerate. The protection level should be matched to the site environment rather than chosen once for every plant.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Control needs split into two groups. On-off service — backwash sequencing, isolation, tank filling — uses solenoid valves and limit switches, and some of it cycles frequently: backwash valves cycle at least daily, and aeration or flow-control valves can move constantly. Modulating services such as flow control, chemical dosing and aeration air regulation need a positioner with continuous feedback. One practical point: quarter-turn actuators fit butterfly and ball valves directly, while gate and globe valves common on water duty are multi-turn and require a linear actuator or a geared conversion — worth confirming before you order the package.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Sizing for water duty follows the same discipline as any other service. Valve torque data from the valve maker — including the effect of seat material and line pressure — is compared against the actuator's output at the plant's air pressure, with a working margin added for the friction and aging that real plants accumulate. Many plants standardize on one or two actuator sizes across services to simplify spare parts, which is practical as long as the largest valve in each group drives the size. Accessories for water service are straightforward: solenoid valves and limit switches for on-off duty, a positioner with feedback on modulating services, and washdown-safe enclosures to protect the electrics in dosing and sludge areas.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 推荐产品表 -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">RECOMMENDED ACTUATORS</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Actuator Families for Water Treatment Duty</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">Actuator family</th>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">Typical duty</th>
                <th class="px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold">When it fits</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/rack-and-pinion/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Filter backwash and isolation valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Double acting or spring return, fast cycling, direct ISO 5211 mount</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/rack-and-pinion/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion + positioner</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Aeration and flow control valves</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Modulating control with position feedback</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/rack-and-pinion/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Rack and pinion, corrosion protected</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Chemical dosing lines</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Epoxy-coated housings, stainless fasteners for aggressive exposure</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-50/60">
                <td class="px-6 py-3 font-medium text-navy-950"><a href="/products/scotch-yoke/" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline">Scotch yoke</a></td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">Large raw water and sludge lines</td>
                <td class="px-6 py-3 text-slate-600">High torque for big bore valves, economical at large sizes</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">PNEUMACTUATOR covers 8 Nm to 200,000 Nm output torque with double acting, spring return and modulating configurations. Weatherproofing and corrosion protection options are confirmed per plant site.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 关键考虑点 -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">KEY CONSIDERATIONS</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">What to Check for Water Treatment Actuation</h2>
        <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Outdoor durability:</span> coating, fasteners and seals should match the site — rain, humidity, UV and washdown all shorten the life of unprotected hardware.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Cycle frequency:</span> backwash valves cycle daily and aeration valves can cycle constantly; confirm the actuator suits the expected cycle rate.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">On-off vs modulating:</span> solenoid and limit switches for on-off; positioner with feedback for flow control and dosing.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Supply air:</span> clean, dry air at stable pressure; many plants share one compressor system with instrumentation.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Valve type:</span> butterfly and ball valves take quarter-turn actuators directly; gate and globe valves need linear actuation or gearing.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Fail-safe:</span> spring return to close or open where isolation of a line matters when air is lost.</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-700"><span class="font-semibold text-navy-950">Feedback to SCADA:</span> limit switches and position transmitters for plant-wide status monitoring.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <div class="mt-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-blue">FAQ</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Water Treatment Actuation Questions</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">How long do pneumatic actuators last outdoors at a water plant?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Service life depends on the environment and the protection chosen: epoxy-coated housings, stainless steel fasteners and sealed enclosures stand up well to rain, humidity and washdown, while unprotected units in the same spot age quickly. Tell us the site conditions and we confirm the material and coating options that fit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Can one actuator do both on-off and modulating duty?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The actuator body can, but the accessories differ. On-off service runs a solenoid valve with limit switches. Modulating service adds a positioner and continuous feedback, and the actuator should be selected for frequent positioning cycles. Specify the control mode up front so the package is built correctly the first time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Which actuator for filter backwash automation?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Backwash sequencing is on-off duty on butterfly or ball valves, typically handled by rack and pinion actuators, double acting or spring return depending on whether a fail-safe position is required. Sizing follows the valve torque at operating pressure, and the sequence runs through solenoid valves under PLC control with limit switch confirmation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Need Actuators for Your Water Treatment Plant?"
    subtitle="Send your valve list, service type, cycle frequency and site conditions — we recommend weatherproof packages within 24 hours. Email sales@pneumactuator.com."
  />
</Layout>
